    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** stands as the definitive anchor of the Zurich Zebras lineup with an elite score of 80.98. While facing a moderate threat in Gusto, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** benefits from a prime leadoff spot and a dynamic platoon advantage that boosts his output significantly; his presence is non-negotiable, particularly given our organizational emphasis on speed as the scarcity leader. Similarly, **Yordan Alvarez** (69.38) and **Kazuma Okamoto** (69.87) provide high-floor stability, with **Kazuma Okamoto** capitalizing on a favorable 5.35 xERA matchup against Gibson, effectively negating the minor platoon regression. **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** also grades out as a strong start at 68.40, as the 6.05 xERA of Van Eyk offers an ideal environment for his power-first profile to flourish.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Chase Meidroth**, who finished just outside the starting rotation with a score of 49.33. While **Chase Meidroth** offered decent utility, his efficiency was capped by a lower spot in the order and a slight negative dynamic platoon adjustment compared to the higher-ceiling profiles of **Junior Caminero**\u2014who remains a lock despite a challenging matchup against the pedigree of Cole\u2014and **Caleb Durbin**. We are carefully monitoring the situation for **Trea Turner** (50.81), whose efficiency is temporarily dampened by a clash with the disciplined Henderson and a defensive environment that limits stolen base upside; however, his elite baseline keeps him firmly in the mix. \n\nRisks remain present across the board, particularly regarding the high-stakes matchup for **Junior Caminero** against Cole and the persistent fragility of our depth, with **Colt Keith** and **Casey Schmitt** still sidelined on the IL. We continue to hold **Gary Sanchez**, **Jacob Gonzalez**, **Hector Rodriguez**, **Luis Pena**, and **Pedro Ramirez** in reserve; none of these names warranted a promotion today given the superior matchups for **Dillon Dingler** and **Lars Nootbaar**, the latter of whom draws a favorable 4.57 xERA start against Adams to solidify his place at the top of our order.",
